these are grace malanez last hours  Auckland city center on the 1st of  December last year the eve of her 22nd  birthday she takes a picture of the  Christmas tree and sends it to her  parents back in the UK grace Mullane was  travelling in New Zealand as part of her  round-the-world trip after finishing  University back home she'd arranged a  date on tinder the dating app here she  meets the man now accused of her murder  the pair first go to a burger bar they  ordered drinks find a table an hour  later shortly after 7:00 p.m. they go on  to another bar here they find a smaller  table the accused who can't be named for  legal reasons puts his hand behind  Grace's head and they kiss for the first  time they continued to drink heavily  at one point miss Mullane messaged a  friend back home she said about the  defendant literally I click with him so  well a friend encouraged her to pursue  it according to a statement read out in  court today miss Mullane replied I will  let you know what happens tomorrow that  message never came at 9:37 p.m. the  couple leave the bar it's only a short  walk to the city life hotel where  they're caught on CCTV three minutes  later they take the lift to the 3rd  floor this is the last moment miss  Mullane is seen alive ms Mullane died by  strangulation the prosecution says it  was murder the defense says it was the  result of a consensual sex act gone  wrong these photographs taken by police  and shown to the jury today show the  hotel room afterwards the white  substance on the floor is luminol used  to detect traces of blood the haunting  images of mr. malanez last movements  tell part of the story of that night but  what happened behind the closed door of  the hotel room where there were no  cameras is the subject of this trial  which continues Tom Cheshire Sky News
 

